4. Expressly permitted activities

The following are permitted even when they generate revenue:

(a) Accepting voluntary donations or tips to support development, maintenance
or distribution, provided payment is not required to obtain Covered Material,
updates or functionality that is offered in connection with the donation.

(b) Running a server using Covered Material with voluntary donation support,
provided access to that server and its Covered Material functionality is free.
Acknowledging supporters is allowed. This exception does not authorize selling
server access, mod features or mod-based in-game benefits.

(c) Creating, publishing and monetizing gameplay videos, streams, reviews,
tutorials and similar audiovisual coverage of Covered Material, including
advertising, sponsorships, viewer subscriptions and tips. This exception covers
the audiovisual work, not selling or licensing the mod or extracted assets.

Businesses and paid employees may exercise the rights in section 2 on the same
terms as other users. Use in employment or to assist a commercial activity is
not prohibited merely because money is earned. A resulting Paid Product still
requires permission if it contains, bundles, incorporates or adapts a protected
